Here is a complete, modular, high-performance, and production-ready implementation of a **Healthcare Patient Monitoring System** in C#. 

This architecture leverages **`System.Threading.Channels`** for low-latency, thread-safe asynchronous processing, completely decoupling telemetry ingestion, statistical analysis, and emergency dispatch.

```
                  ┌──────────────────────────────┐
                  │   Patient Sensors (Sim)      │
                  └──────────────┬───────────────┘
                                 │ Telemetry
                                 ▼
┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│ LAYER 1: VITAL SIGNS INGESTER                                   │
│  - Receives telemetry                                           │
│  - Rejects corrupted/physically impossible data                │
└──────────────────────────────┬──────────────────────────────────┘
                               │ Channel<TelemetryPayload>
                               ▼
┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│ LAYER 2: ANOMALY DETECTION ENGINE                               │
│  - Maintains a thread-safe sliding window per patient           │
│  - Calculates Rolling Mean (μ) and Standard Deviation (σ)       │
│  - Catches rapid degradation (Z-Score) & absolute limits        │
└──────────────────────────────┬──────────────────────────────────┘
                               │ Channel<AnomalyAlert>
                               ▼
┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│ LAYER 3: EMERGENCY DISPATCH SUBSYSTEM                           │
│  - Consumes high-priority alerts                                │
│  - Sends notifications via resilient SMS/Email channels         │
│  - Handles failures gracefully with Exponential Backoff + Jitter│
└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
```

